            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "engine/review/app/check.go: exemptedHead reads the stored exemption, decodes it, and re-applies review.CheckExemption (high-risk and report-clear rules) before the file is trusted. A stored file edited after Exempt wrote it therefore cannot clear a head.",
              "engine/review/app/check.go: the stored binding is validated by DecodeExemption before its base is passed to bind and git. The test in check_exempt_test.go that forges a base shaped like a command-line option asserts ErrInvalidBinding and that git is never called with it, so no option-injection path is visible.",
              "engine/review/app/check.go: the candidate is recomputed from git for the stored base and the delivered head, and CheckBinding requires it to equal the stored binding. Exemption files cannot be reused for a different diff, and exemptions for another head are skipped by their binding rather than by their name.",
              "engine/review/app/check.go: every error path in the exemption flow returns Checked{} with a refusal, so a read, decode, or git failure does not clear the head. Whether a blocking or not-clear result wins over an exemption is decided in review.Cleared, which is outside this candidate. The new tests assert that behavior, so I could not verify it here.",
              "engine/review/app/check_exempt_test.go: test-only addition. It uses fakes and adds no secrets, dependencies, or runtime surface."
            ]
          }
        }
