            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "engine/review/app/check.go: exemptedHead decodes the stored file, applies CheckExemption, and then compares the binding head. It recomputes the candidate from git and applies CheckBinding. Every failure returns an error, so a malformed or edited exemption refuses the head rather than clearing it.",
              "engine/review/app/check.go: Check passes both results and exemptions to review.Cleared. Per the doc comment, a result that blocks or is not clear wins over an exemption. Check returns an empty Checked on any error.",
              "engine/review/app/check_exempt_test.go: tests cover clearing by an exemption alone, round-trip with Exempt, ordering of numbers 2 and 10, a head with both a result and an exemption, and a blocking, unchecked or not-run result beating an exemption. They also cover edited risk or report, a binding mismatch on diff or paths, git and store failures, exemptions of another head including a name collision, and a forged option-like base that never reaches git. Each asserts the error, the message content, an empty answer and no store writes.",
              "Limitation: the review is confined to the two supplied patches, so the helper functions in review (ExemptionsOfHead, Cleared) and the fakes were not visible. No defect is evident from the visible code."
